Settings → Staff: table (Name, Role, Access, MFA, Status) and "Add staff member": role picker with descriptions (receptionist, nurse, care coordinator, practice admin; doctors redirected to Add doctor) → facility scope and hours → permissions (locked rows from the role cannot be granted/removed here) → invite. Custom roles composed from capabilities.
ac:
- Choosing "Doctor" shows "Doctors need licence verification. Use Settings → Doctors → Add doctor." and does not create a staff membership.
- Locked permissions from a built-in role are displayed but not editable; custom roles cannot exceed the capabilities of practice admin.
- The invite uses the P0 flow; the staff table shows invited/active/suspended/offboarded and MFA enrolment state.
- Every permission change is written to the audit log ("Every change is written to the audit log").
- A receptionist created here cannot open clinical endpoints (security test reused from P0).

=== MDV-P1-009
title: Staff offboarding removes access immediately and ends all sessions
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E03
prd: P1-11
screens: F-10
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin
labels: staff, security, lifecycle
estimate: 1
weeks: 6
depends: MDV-P1-008, MDV-P0-012
confidence: 90 | Requirement is explicit and session revocation exists from P0.
sources: PRD v2 P1-11
desc:
"Offboard" on a staff member sets membership to offboarded, revokes all sessions and devices for that tenant, cancels pending invites, reassigns or flags their open items (none clinical yet in P1), and records reason and actor.
ac:
- After offboarding, the next request from any of the person's sessions in that tenant fails within 60 seconds and they cannot sign in to that tenant.
- Memberships in other tenants are unaffected.
- The action requires confirmation, a reason, and is audited.
- The last practice admin cannot offboard themselves (prevents lock-out).

=== MDV-P1-010
title: Licence/registration expiry reminders and quarterly access review prompt
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E03
prd: P1-11
priority: MUST
roles: Practice owner
labels: compliance, jobs
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 7
depends: MDV-P1-007, MDV-P1-032
confidence: 85 | Requirement explicit; uses Hangfire jobs from MDV-P1-032.
sources: PRD v2 P1-11; design/Medvya Enterprise Pages (H-03 "Quarterly access review due")
desc:
Scheduled job notifies owners 60/30/7 days before a doctor licence or facility registration expires and on expiry (doctor recording/signing then disabled again). Quarterly access review: owners get a task listing every active membership, role and last sign-in; they confirm or offboard each and the completion is recorded.
ac:
- Expiry notifications are sent at 60/30/7/0 days and appear in the notification centre (D-03) and by email.
- On expiry, capabilities that require a verified licence are disabled server-side until renewed and re-verified.
- The quarterly review lists all memberships and records a decision per person; completion date is shown in settings.
- Both jobs are idempotent and audited.

