title: Schedule templates: working hours, breaks, slot length per service, per-location calendars, time zones
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E04
prd: P1-04
screens: P-04
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin, Doctor
labels: scheduling
estimate: 3
weeks: 5-6
depends: MDV-P1-005, MDV-P1-007
confidence: 80 | Behaviour clear from PRD and schedule design; slot-per-service rules need a short refinement (service catalogue fully arrives in P4).
sources: PRD v2 P1-04; design/Medvya Clinician App (Schedule, settings hours); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#schedule-p-04--medvya-clinician-app
desc:
Per doctor and location: weekly template (weekday, start, end, room/resource), breaks (e.g. lunch), default slot length (15/20/30 min) and per-visit-type length (e.g. new consult 40 min = 2 slots). Facility time zone; all times stored UTC and displayed in facility time. Resources (procedure room) can be scheduled like a doctor column. Generates bookable slots on the fly (no pre-materialised slot table required) or materialises slots per day — decision recorded.
ac:
- Given a template Mon–Fri 09:00–13:00 and 17:00–20:00 with 20-minute slots, then the calendar shows bookable slots exactly in those windows in facility local time.
- Breaks and closed days show as Unavailable (hatched) with the reason and cannot be booked.
- Changing a template affects only future unbooked slots; existing appointments outside new hours are listed for action.
- Visit types can span multiple slots and the calendar renders them spanning.
- Daylight-saving-free zones (IST, GST) and a test zone with DST are handled correctly (unit tests).

=== MDV-P1-012
title: Leave and schedule exceptions with re-offer of affected appointments
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E04
prd: P1-04
screens: P-04
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin, Doctor, Receptionist
labels: scheduling
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 6
depends: MDV-P1-011, MDV-P1-021
confidence: 82 | Designed message "6 booked patients will be offered new slots before leave is saved".
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (Settings hours leave notice)
desc:
Add leave (from, to, reason) or one-off exceptions (extra session, shortened day). Before saving, the system lists booked patients in the range; reception chooses to offer new slots (sends rebooking message with link/phone) or reschedule manually. Leave is saved only after each affected appointment has an action.
ac:
- Saving leave that overlaps booked appointments shows the count and list and requires an action per appointment before save.
- Affected patients receive a rebooking message (no clinical details) and the appointments move to "needs rebooking" on the board.
- Extra sessions create bookable slots for that day only.
- Leave and exceptions are audited.

=== MDV-P1-013
status: In progress
progress:
- Merged [PR #40](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/40): Patients module back end — India rules (minimum fields, ABHA optional, Aadhaar last 4 only, PIN, payer kinds), facility-scoped MRN, write and audit in one transaction (fail closed), audited reads, ABHA Always Encrypted with exact lookup
- Left: endpoints and UI (P-02), consents (MDV-P1-019), family (MDV-P1-020), duplicates (MDV-P1-016)
title: Patient registration — India full flow (identity, ABHA optional, Aadhaar last 4, Indian address, payer)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E05
prd: P1-05
screens: P-02
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist
labels: registration, india
estimate: 4
weeks: 5-6
depends: MDV-P0-009, MDV-P0-017
confidence: 88 | Hi-fi P-02 with interactive validation rules and data map; ABHA verification via ABDM is manual entry in P1 (API in P8).
sources: design/Medvya Patient Registration; docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#patient-registration-p-02--medvya-patient-registration
desc:
/patients/new full mode, India: steps Identity & IDs → Contact & address → Family & emergency (MDV-P1-020) → Payer → Consents (MDV-P1-019) → Review (MDV-P1-016). Identity: first/last name, DOB or age ("estimated"), sex at birth, optional gender identity, preferred language, ABHA number (14 digits) and address (optional, manual entry; "Verify with ABHA" banner shows the P8 path as disabled/coming later), other ID type with Aadhaar last 4 only. Contact: mobile (required), alternate, email, house/flat, street, city, district, state/UT, PIN (6 digits), country. Payer: self-pay / corporate / private insurance (TPA) / government scheme (reference only). Side panel shows preview card and "Data map · this step writes".
ac:
- Minimum to register (India): name, DOB or age, sex, mobile; other fields optional; validation messages match the design (e.g. "PIN code must be 6 digits").
- Aadhaar can only be stored as last 4 digits; entering 12 digits is rejected with an explanation; ABHA is stored via Always Encrypted and is never required for care.
- On save, PATIENT (demographics), PATIENT_IDENTIFIER (tokenised), PAYER_COVERAGE, CONSENT_RECEIPT and AUDIT_EVENT PatientRegistered.v1 (no PHI in payload) are written in one transaction and a facility-scoped MRN is assigned.
- The success screen shows name, MRN, timestamp and actor and offers Book appointment · Check in now (walk-in) · Register another.
- The receptionist cannot see any clinical data from the registration or directory screens (security test).
- Form is keyboard-completable, errors announced via aria-live, works at tablet width.

