- Completing the missing fields later closes the task automatically.
- Duplicate check (MDV-P1-016) still runs in quick mode.

=== MDV-P1-016
status: In progress
progress:
- [PR #61](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/61) (in review): possible match = exact ABHA/EID/passport (deterministic Always Encrypted) or similar name + identical non-estimated DOB, never phone; privacy-safe candidates (initials, age, masked IDs); registration re-checks and saves nothing until resolved (quick mode too); decisions stored as MergeRequest (NotSame / Proposed) and audited with the actor; `POST /v1/patients/duplicate-check` and `POST /v1/patients` (Full access, facility from the session); quick form with debounced warning, review panel and "Resolve duplicate to save", en/hi/ar RTL, axe clean
- Tested on SQL Server (duplicate-check p95 10 ms with 50,000 synthetic patients locally); 13 mutations each caught
- Left: merge review queue, approval and suppression of "not the same" pairs (MDV-P1-017); real sessions need MDV-P0-012; thresholds to tune on pilot data
title: Duplicate warning while typing and duplicate resolution before save
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E05
prd: P1-05
screens: P-02
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist
labels: registration, dedup, safety
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 6
depends: MDV-P1-013
confidence: 85 | Matching rule and UI are designed; scoring thresholds need tuning on pilot data.
sources: design/Medvya Patient Registration (Review & duplicate check); design/Medvya Gap Analysis (G-04 "Duplicate warning while typing" MUST)
desc:
As name + DOB (and identifiers) are typed, call /v1/patients/duplicate-check (debounced) and show "Possible match" inline. On the Review step, a side-by-side NEW vs EXISTING panel ("Attention · possible existing record. Matched on name + date of birth. A shared phone number alone is never treated as a match.") with actions: Not the same person · continue / Use existing record / Request merge review (P-03). Save is blocked ("Resolve duplicate to save") until one is chosen.
ac:
- A candidate is suggested when name similarity + identical DOB, or an exact identifier (ABHA/EID/passport) match exists; phone-only matches never produce a suggestion (test).
- Duplicate-check responses show initials, age and masked identifiers only, never full details of the other record until "Use existing record" is chosen.
- Save remains disabled until the receptionist resolves the duplicate; the decision and actor are audited.
- "Use existing record" opens that patient without creating a new one; "Request merge review" creates a merge request (MDV-P1-017).
- p95 duplicate-check latency < 300 ms on staging data of 50,000 synthetic patients.

=== MDV-P1-017
title: Duplicate / merge review with second approver when both records hold clinical data (P-03)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E05
prd: P1-05
screens: P-03
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist, Practice admin, Doctor
labels: dedup, merge, safety
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 7
depends: MDV-P1-016
confidence: 82 | Designed; reversibility (unmerge) is formally required in P5-02 but the data model must allow it now.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (P-03); docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#merge-request-p1p5
desc:
/patients/merge: side-by-side comparison (name, DOB, sex, mobile, ABHA/EID, visits, allergies) with actions Not the same person / Request clinician approval. Merge executes only after approval; when both records have clinical data (from P2 on) a second approver (clinician) is required. Merge keeps both originals, maps the loser to the survivor and is reversible.
ac:
- "Not the same person" closes the request and suppresses the same pair from future suggestions.
- A merge without the required approver(s) is impossible (server-side), and approvals are audited.
- After merge, searching either MRN finds the surviving record; appointments and identifiers move; the merge can be undone by an admin within the retention period.
- Merge history is visible on the patient record.

