title: Create an appointment from the calendar with a short slot hold
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E06
prd: P1-06, P1-07
screens: P-04
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist, Doctor
labels: booking
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 6-7
depends: MDV-P1-011, MDV-P1-018
confidence: 88 | Designed interaction (click empty slot → book); hold mechanism specified in P1-07.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (Schedule); PRD v2 P1-06, P1-07
desc:
Clicking an empty slot opens the booking panel for that doctor/resource and time; select or register a patient, visit type (sets length), reason category (free-text reason never shown on reception screens beyond category), channel. A slot hold (default 2 minutes) reserves the slot while the receptionist completes the form; confirmation creates the appointment and triggers the confirmation message (MDV-P1-032).
ac:
- Opening the booking panel creates a hold; another user trying the same slot sees it as "being booked" and cannot confirm it.
- Holds expire automatically after the configured time and the slot becomes free.
- A booking for an unavailable column (doctor not working) is impossible from UI and API.
- Booking writes AppointmentBooked.v1 (no PHI) and an audit event; the appointment appears on the board in Booked.
- Booking API p95 < 300 ms under the P1 load profile (MDV-P1-037).

=== MDV-P1-022
status: In progress
progress:
- Open [PR #60](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/60) (stacked on #59): SCHEDULE_SLOT rows per 5-minute unit with a unique index on (calendar, location, slot start); every hold and booking in a SERIALIZABLE transaction after `sp_getapplock` per doctor-day; deadlocks and lock timeouts retried, then "busy"; 100 parallel bookings or holds of one slot give exactly one on Testcontainers SQL Server (also overlapping multi-slot); mutation-checked (unique index, lock, all guards: 16 double bookings without them)
- Left: the 100-parallel run on staging (needs MDV-P0-006); freeing slots on cancel/no-show/reschedule (MDV-P1-024)
title: No double booking under concurrency (unique index, serializable transaction, doctor-day app lock)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E06
prd: P1-07
covers: exit:2
priority: MUST
roles: System
labels: booking, concurrency, safety
estimate: 2
weeks: 7
depends: MDV-P1-021
confidence: 90 | Mechanism fully specified by PRD v2; test is explicit in the exit gate.
sources: PRD v2 P1-07, exit 2; docs/03-architecture/data-model.md#key-constraints
desc:
Filtered unique index on (doctor_id, location_id, slot_start) for non-cancelled appointments; booking inside a SERIALIZABLE transaction with sp_getapplock on "doctor:{id}:{date}"; the frontend check is only a convenience. Multi-slot visits reserve every covered slot.
ac:
- An automated test fires 100 parallel booking attempts at one slot; exactly one succeeds and 99 receive a clear "slot no longer available" error (exit gate 2), on Testcontainers SQL Server and on staging.
- Overlapping multi-slot bookings are rejected the same way.
- Deadlocks/lock timeouts are retried safely without creating duplicates.
- The test runs in CI on every PR touching Scheduling.

