depends: MDV-P1-021, MDV-P1-019
confidence: 86 | Stack decided (Hangfire on Azure SQL, ACS); template rules defined.
sources: PRD v2 P1-09, P1 NFR 2; docs/03-architecture/integrations.md
desc:
Hangfire server (Worker.Jobs) on Azure SQL in its own schema/user — no Redis or Service Bus in P1. Email provider: SendGrid (founder decision 20 Oct 2026, free tier) behind the Notifications adapter; Azure Communication Services remains an alternative. Events: booking confirmation, reschedule, cancellation, 24 h and 2 h reminders, leave rebooking. Templates per tenant/language without clinical details. NOTIFICATION and NOTIFICATION_ATTEMPT record provider id, delivery state and retries with backoff; reminders are cancelled when the appointment changes.
ac:
- Booking triggers a confirmation within 1 minute; reminders are sent at 24 h and 2 h before (facility time), respecting quiet hours and channel consent.
- Rescheduling or cancelling cancels pending reminders and sends the right message once (idempotency test).
- Delivery status (queued, sent, delivered, failed, bounced) is stored and visible to reception for each appointment.
- Failed sends are retried with backoff up to the configured limit and then shown as failed on the board/notification centre.
- Hangfire dashboard is only reachable by Medvya operations through authenticated admin route; no Redis or Service Bus resources exist in P1 infrastructure.

=== MDV-P1-033
title: SMS confirmations and reminders with India DLT templates and delivery receipts
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E08
prd: P1-09
covers: dep:2, exit:4
priority: MUST
roles: Patient, Receptionist
labels: notifications, sms, india
estimate: 2
weeks: 8
depends: MDV-P1-032, MDV-P1-045
confidence: 68 | Depends on DLT sender/template registration (external lead time) and the SMS provider decision (open question Q-03).
sources: PRD v2 P1-09, dependency 2; docs/01-prd/source-conflicts.md (Q-03)
desc:
SMS adapter (Azure Communication Services where supported, otherwise a DLT-registered aggregator) behind the Notifications interface. India messages use the registered DLT template IDs and sender; UAE uses its approved sender. Delivery receipts update NOTIFICATION_ATTEMPT. Reminder delivery rate is computed per clinic.
ac:
- SMS uses only registered templates; a message not matching a registered template is not sent (validation test).
- Delivery receipts are processed (webhook verified/authenticated) and update status; failures are visible to reception.
- Delivery rate dashboard shows ≥ 98 % delivered during the pilot or lists every failure with reason (exit gate 4).
- Messages contain no clinical details; sender name is the clinic's.

=== MDV-P1-034
title: Notification centre for staff (D-03), push-safe content
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E08
prd: P1-09
screens: D-03
priority: MUST
roles: All staff
labels: notifications, ui
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 8
depends: MDV-P1-032, MDV-P0-022
confidence: 85 | Overlay is designed with the push rule; event list for P1 is small (failed reminders, expiries, access requests, rebooking needed).
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (Notifications overlay); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#notification-centre-d-03
desc:
Bell with count opens an overlay listing in-app notifications (kind, title, time) with "Mark all read". P1 events: reminder failed, leave rebooking needed, licence expiring, access request, quarterly access review due. Browser/phone push (optional) uses the generic text only.
ac:
- Notifications are scoped to the user's tenant/facility and role.
- Push or browser notifications never include patient names or results; content is "New update from {clinic}. Open Medvya to view." (test on payload).
- Mark all read and per-item read state persist across devices.
- Overlay is keyboard accessible and screen-reader friendly.

=== MDV-P1-035
title: Practice access log for owners (F-12): who opened which record and when
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E09
prd: P1-10
screens: F-12
priority: MUST
roles: Practice owner
labels: audit, settings
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 8
depends: MDV-P0-017
confidence: 84 | Requirement explicit; screen listed in inventory (/settings/audit) but its detail data was in the truncated part of the design.
sources: PRD v2 P1-10; design/Medvya Foundations inventory (F-12)
desc:
/settings/audit: filter by staff member, patient (search), action, date range; shows time, actor, role, action, patient (name visible to the owner after selecting), purpose and outcome (allowed/denied). Export to CSV (watermarked, audited).
ac:
- Only practice owners/admins can open the log (403 for others, audited).
- Filtering by patient lists every read and write of that patient's record by anyone, with timestamps.
- Denied attempts (e.g. receptionist opening a clinical note) appear with outcome "Denied".
- Exports are audited and watermarked with exporter and time.
- Query p95 < 600 ms for a 30-day range in the pilot volume.

