=== MDV-P1-037
title: Performance budget and load test for booking and calendar
type: Task
epic: MDV-P1-E06
prd: P1-06, P1-07
covers: nfr:1
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: performance
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 9
depends: MDV-P1-022, MDV-P1-023
confidence: 86 | Targets explicit; tool choice (k6/NBomber) open but trivial.
sources: PRD v2 P1 NFR 1, X6
desc:
Load profile for two clinics plus headroom (e.g. 20 concurrent receptionists, 200 bookings/hour, board subscriptions). Measure booking API p95, search p95, board load, calendar first render on throttled 4G. Add the budgets to CI (nightly) with alerts on regression.
ac:
- Booking API p95 < 300 ms and reads p95 < 300 ms / writes < 600 ms under the profile on staging.
- Calendar first render < 2.5 s on a typical clinic PC profile over 4G throttling.
- Nightly performance job fails and alerts on > 20 % regression.

=== MDV-P1-038
title: P1 security review: threat-model update, ASVS checks, authorisation tests, dependency scan — no open high/critical
type: Gate
epic: MDV-P1-E10
prd: P1-05, P1-11
covers: exit:5
priority: MUST
roles: Developer, external reviewer (part-time)
labels: security, gate
estimate: 2
weeks: 9
depends: MDV-P1-019, MDV-P1-009, MDV-P1-035
confidence: 80 | Process clear; using a part-time external reviewer (Build Plan advice) depends on availability.
sources: PRD v2 P1 exit 5; design/Medvya Build Plan (direction advice: part-time security reviewer)
desc:
Before real demographics enter production: update the threat model for P1 features (public site, registration, booking, messaging, TV display), run ASVS L2 checks, the authorisation matrix tests, IDOR tests on patient and appointment endpoints, DAST against staging, dependency/container scan, and a short external review of security-sensitive code.
ac:
- No open high or critical findings; mediums have dated remediation tickets.
- IDOR test suite covers every P1 endpoint taking a patient/appointment id.
- Public endpoints (landing, demo, TV display, webhooks) are rate-limited and pass DAST.
- The review report is stored in docs/compliance and linked in R1 release notes.

