=== MDV-P1-041
title: Baseline metrics capture and in-product measurement (check-in time, no-shows, double bookings, reminder delivery)
type: Task
epic: MDV-P1-E10
prd: P1-08, P1-09
covers: pkg:4, exit:3
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Practice owner
labels: metrics
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 9-10
depends: MDV-P1-028, MDV-P1-033
confidence: 84 | Metrics and methods are defined in PRD v2 §06; clinic pre-Medvya baseline needs manual capture.
sources: PRD v2 §06 metrics; docs/01-prd/cross-cutting-metrics-process.md
desc:
Capture each clinic's pre-Medvya baseline (no-show rate, check-in time, double-booking incidents) during the first 2 weeks, and instrument: check-in time (arrival → checked in) median, no-show rate, double-booking constraint violations, reminder delivery rate. Owner-facing mini report (full reports P4).
ac:
- Baseline values per clinic are recorded with method and dates.
- Median check-in time for returning patients is computed from event timestamps and is ≤ 60 s during the measured pilot weeks (exit gate 3) or the gap is reported.
- Metrics contain no PHI and are visible to owners.

=== MDV-P1-042
title: R1 pilot (2 consecutive weeks of real bookings), exit gate review and release notes
type: Gate
epic: MDV-P1-E10
prd: P1-06, P1-08
covers: exit:1, exit:2, exit:3, exit:4, exit:5
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Clinical advisor, pilot users
labels: release, gate, pilot
estimate: 2
weeks: 10
depends: MDV-P1-039, MDV-P1-040, MDV-P1-041, MDV-P1-022, MDV-P1-038
confidence: 65 | Week 10 ends 01 Jan 2027; year-end holidays may prevent "2 consecutive weeks" in-window (open question Q-08).
sources: PRD v2 §08 release process, P1 exit criteria; docs/01-prd/roadmap.md (calendar risks)
desc:
Pilot on flags with daily check-ins in week one, then exit gate review with evidence: two consecutive weeks of real bookings without paper fallback at both clinics; double-booking test result; median check-in; reminder delivery ≥ 98 % with failures visible; no open high/critical findings. Publish R1 release notes and known issues; turn J3 front-desk steps green in the journey specs.
ac:
- Evidence for each of the five exit criteria is attached and confirmed by founder, clinical advisor and one pilot user.
- If the holiday period prevents two consecutive weeks, the gate is formally moved to the first two full January weeks and recorded (no silent slip).
- R1 release notes list P1-01…P1-12 delivered status, known issues and what is not included (clinical notes, Rx, billing, AI, portal).
- Journey J3 front-desk steps (P-01, P-02, P-03) pass in Playwright.

